<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="34808543">&lt;p&gt;
    A grouping of objects that require custom development because they are not readily available out of the box by the
    package. Also known as RICEF or FRICEW.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Reports: regular or ad-hoc documents generated by the package for various information or analytic purposes
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Interfaces: a &quot;live&quot; interface between two or more applications. In complicated business transactions, interfaces
        to other applications may be involved
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Conversions: copying or transferring data from a source system to the target system
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Extensions: a customization where a core package function is given additional capability beyond what comes with
        standard package functionality (out of the box). These are typically developed using the scripting capability that
        is provided with the package
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Forms: data entry forms used with the package for various operational purposes.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Workflows: orchestration of multiple functions in order to complete an end-to-end service for a customer. Processes
        may operate over several hours, weeks or even months (e.g., loan approval)
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
